Changes since v1:
  - Gate the scheduler hooks on TARGET_ARCV_RHX100 directly instead of
    riscv_fusion_enabled_p (RISCV_FUSE_ARCV); dropped the RISCV_FUSE_ARCV
    umbrella and the riscv_fusion_enabled_p forward declaration in
    riscv.cc.
  - Removed the custom arcv_next_fusible_insn helper and use the generic
    next_nonnote_nondebug_insn_bb instead.
  - Call the generic riscv_macro_fusion_pair_p (the table dispatcher)
    instead of arcv_macro_fusion_pair_p, which no longer exists after the
    fusion rework.
  - arcv_sched_adjust_priority and arcv_sched_variable_issue now use
    next_nonnote_nondebug_insn_bb + single_set instead of next_insn +
    INSN_P, dropping the manual DEBUG/USE/CLOBBER guards.
  - reorder2's single-instruction fallback now updates
    cached_can_issue_more in both the memory and ALU branches.
  - Dropped the bogus riscv.h ChangeLog entry: TARGET_ARCV_RHX100 is now
    defined by the fusion patch, so this patch no longer touches riscv.h.
  - Un-XFAIL'd arcv-fusion-ls-update-dump.c and
    arcv-fusion-ls-update-rev-dump.c now that RHX-100 scheduling is
    implemented (no test changes in v1).
